<title>USA: BNFL team wins $1.18 billion U.S. DOE contract.</title>
<headline>BNFL team wins $1.18 billion U.S. DOE contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Energy Department said Friday it had awarded a $1.18 billion contract to a team led by BNFL Inc to treat mixed waste at the Idaho National Engineering Laboratory.</p>
<p>BNFL, a British state-owned company, is the prime contractor, with subcontracts to BNFL Engineering Ltd, GTS Duratek Inc, Manufacturing Sciences Corp, Morrison Knudsen Corp, Pajarito Scientific Corp, Rocky Mountain Remediation Services, and Science Applications International Corp, the department said.</p>
</text>
